      "translations": {
        "en": "Ali ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Hammad ibn Isa, from Hariz, from Zurara, who said:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) مَا حَدُّ الْجِزْيَةِ عَلَى أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ وَ هَلْ عَلَيْهِمْ فِي ذَلِكَ شَيْمْ فِي ذَلِكَ شَيْ‏ءٌ مُوَظَّفٌ لَا يَنْبَغِي أَنْ يَجُوزُوا إِلَى غَيْرِهِ فَقَالَ ذَاكَ إِلَى الْإِمَامِ أَنْ يَأْخُذَ مِنْ كُلِّ إِنْسَانٍ مِنْهُمْ مَا شَاءَ عَلَى قَدْرِ مَالِهِ بِمَا يُطِيقُ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "I said to Abu Abdullah (peace be upon him), 'What is the limit of the jizya upon the People of the Book, and is there anything fixed upon them regarding that which is not befitting for them to exceed to something else?' He (peace be upon him) said: 'That is up to the Imam to take from every person from them whatever he desires, in accordance with his wealth, according to what he can endure.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "إِنَّمَا هُمْ قَوْمٌ فَدَوْا أَنْفُسَهُمْ مِنْ أَنْ يُسْتَعْبَدُوا أَوْ يُقْتَلُوا فَالْجِزْيَةُ تُؤْخَذُ مِنْهُمْ عَلَى قَدْرِ مَا يُطِيقُونَ لَهُ أَنْ يَأْخُذَهُمْ بِهِ حَتَّى يُسْلِمُوا فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ تَبَارَكَ وَ تَعَالَى قَالَ حَتَّى يُعْطُوا الْجِزْيَةَ عَنْ يَدٍ وَ هُمْ صَاغِرُونَ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "They are a people who ransomed themselves from being enslaved or killed, so the jizya is taken from them according to what they can endure, to the extent that he can seize them with it until they become Muslim. Indeed, Allah, Blessed and High, said: 'Until they pay the jizya with their own hands, and they are humbled.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "وَكَيْفَ يَكُونُ صَاغِرًا وَ هُوَ لَا يَكْتَرِثُ لِمَا يُؤْخَذُ مِنْهُ حَتَّى يَجِدَ ذُلًّا لِمَا أُخِذَ مِنْهُ فَيَأْلَمَ لِذَلِكَ فَيُسْلِمَ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "And how can he be humbled if he does not care about what is taken from him, until he finds humiliation in what was taken from him, so he feels pain because of it, and thus becomes Muslim."
      }
    },
